# AI BlackBox Flight Recorder - Orchestrator venv: direct dependencies
#
# This is the human-edited manifest. Nothing installs it directly. After an
# edit, run `scripts/compile_python_lock.sh`, which regenerates:
#   requirements.lock.txt  the full closure, every package == pinned with its
#                          sha256 hashes. Scripts/install.sh and the in-app
#                          updater install it with `pip install --require-hashes`.
#   requirements.txt       the same pins without hashes, for installs that
#                          cannot use hash mode (combined with
#                          requirements.dev.txt, or an updater older than the lock).
# CI (.github/workflows/supply-chain.yml) fails when either file is out of sync
# with this one, runs pip-audit against the lock, and runs
# scripts/check_imports_vs_manifest.py.
# Dev-only packages live in requirements.dev.txt. The MCP server has its own
# venv and manifest (MCP/requirements.txt).
#
# Rules:
#   - Every third-party import in Orchestrator/ and ToolVault/ is declared
#     here, including lazy imports behind `except ImportError`, and every entry
#     is imported. An entry that is not imported says why in a tag:
#       [transitive]  a dependency's dependency, declared for its security
#                     floor or a compatibility cap
#       [runtime]     loaded by name, not by an import statement
#   - Packages at 1.0 or later are capped below their next major. 0.x
#     packages are capped below 1, or below their next minor where a minor
#     release breaks us (httpx). The web stack stays at its validated versions
#     until its upgrade lands (audit rank 70).
#   - A security floor is the first release with the fix. Floors are what
#     move an EXISTING box: pip leaves an installed version that satisfies a
#     requirement alone. Raise a floor when an advisory lands.
#
# If the hashed install fails on a box (no wheel for its platform, a proxy
# rewriting downloads), the installer and the updater stop with an error.
# Nothing falls back by itself. The manual fallback is
# `Orchestrator/venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt` (same pins, no hash
# check); run pip-audit on the venv afterwards.

# === Web framework / ASGI: held at the validated versions (upgrade: rank 70) ===
# Starlette 0.48 carries advisories fixed only in 0.49.1 and 1.x
# (CVE-2025-62727, CVE-2026-48710, -48817, -48818, -54282, -54283). fastapi
# 0.118 requires starlette<0.49, so they close with the fastapi upgrade; the
# pip-audit gate lists them as known exceptions until then.
fastapi==0.118.0
starlette==0.48.0
uvicorn[standard]==0.30.0
pydantic==2.9.0
python-multipart>=0.0.32,<0.1   # [runtime] starlette's form parser (File/Form uploads); CVE-2024-53981, CVE-2026-24486, -40347, -42561, -53538..-53540

